-- #822 control pair, REJECT half.  `Box`'s first parameter is PHANTOM — no field
-- uses it in an effect position — so it is Type-kinded and `Box e Unit` pins
-- NOTHING about <e> (a Type-kinded var and a Row-kinded one may share a spelling
-- and still be independent variables).  <e> therefore rides only the callback, and
-- an impl applying it performs <e> on no declared row: T-EFFECT-ARG-UNCOVERED.
-- Its sibling graded_ctor_row_arg_ok.mdk differs by ONE constructor field and is
-- accepted — the pair is what proves the kind, not the spelling, decides.
data Box e a = Mk a

interface GM t where
  gm : t -> (Unit -> <e> Unit) -> Box e Unit -> Box e Unit
